---
description: How to use the Virlo MCP tools correctly (intent-first research, async job polling, credit awareness)
alwaysApply: true
---

virlo-api-usage:

- Always check `get_credit_balance` before starting a paid research run.
- Never invent search keywords from a topic directly. Write a concrete one-sentence intent first (goal + content type + exclusions), then call `suggest_keywords` with that intent. If `quality.passes` is false, sharpen the intent and retry before searching.
- Creation tools (`search_keywords`, `create_niche_monitor`, `lookup_creator`, `analyze_video`, etc.) wait up to ~25 seconds and then return a `job_id` if still running. Agent runs usually finish collecting in about 8 minutes (9 in 10 within 20). Tell the user it is running and check again on their next message; never call a status tool repeatedly in a row.
- Treat `finalized: true` as the done signal, not `status === "completed"`: a job can be "completed" with secondary AI analysis still pending. `partial_failure` is still usable data.
- Read tools (`get_keyword_search_results`, `get_niche_monitor_data`, `get_satellite_run`) are free to call repeatedly: filter by date/platform/min_views at read time rather than re-running a paid search. Instant data reads (trends, sounds, hooks, hashtags, `raw_*`) are billed per call even when empty.
- Prefer `order_by=weighted_score` (or `rising`/`growth` where offered) over raw view counts when ranking creators, sounds, or hashtags: raw views over-favor already-viral content.
- Recurring agents (`create_niche_monitor`, the tool name for recurring Content Research Agents) bill per run (`$0.50/run`, `+$1.00/run` with Data Intelligence). One-shot agents (`search_keywords`) bill once (`$0.50`, `+$1.00` with Data Intelligence). Confirm cadence and cost with the user before creating a recurring monitor.
